# Copy to ops/.env and fill in. ops/.env is gitignored and must never be committed.
#
# PLACEFY_JWT_SECRET signs access tokens (HS256), so it needs at least 32 bytes of real
# entropy. The placeholder below is not a key and the application will reject it at startup.
# Generate one:
#
#   bash        openssl rand -base64 48
#   PowerShell  [Convert]::ToBase64String((1..48 | ForEach-Object { Get-Random -Max 256 }))
#
# Changing it invalidates every issued access token, which is the intended way to revoke
# them all at once.

PLACEFY_JWT_SECRET=replace-me-with-at-least-32-bytes-of-real-entropy

# Published host ports. Defaults are 5432 / 8080 / 5173; override any that clash with
# something else already running on your machine. The frontend's API base URL and the
# backend's allowed CORS origin follow these automatically.
# PLACEFY_DB_PORT=5432
# PLACEFY_API_PORT=8080
# PLACEFY_WEB_PORT=5173
